# Secrets for config/deploy.yml. Safe for git; values are fetched at deploy time
# from Bitwarden Secrets Manager by the machine running `kamal` (it needs `bws`
# and BWS_ACCESS_TOKEN). Every key below must exist in the Bitwarden store
# under exactly this name, and must match config/deploy.yml env.secret. Add a
# key only when code reads it.
#
# This repository is public. Never write a value in this file.
SECRETS=$(kamal secrets fetch --adapter bitwarden-sm all)
# Kamal shell-escapes the fetched JSON, so $SECRETS must stay UNQUOTED below: quoted, the
# backslashes survive and `secrets extract` fails with JSON::ParserError.

# The token /feedback files GitHub issues with (crates/open-server/src/github.rs).
# A fine-grained personal access token for wenmar-pro/wenmar-open with only
# "Issues: read and write".
OPEN_GITHUB_TOKEN=$(kamal secrets extract OPEN_GITHUB_TOKEN $SECRETS)
